---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';

const title = 'Terms of Use | NoWatermark';
const description =
  'Terms for using NoWatermark: no guarantees of undetectability, you must have rights to the content you process, and disclosure obligations remain yours.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonicalPath="/terms">
  <div class="nw-shell-narrow pt-8">
    <Breadcrumbs trail={[{ href: '/terms', label: 'Terms' }]} />

    <header class="mt-6">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold">Terms of use</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-lg nw-muted">
        Plain-language terms. The important ones are about what our results do and do not mean.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="nw-content mt-10">
      <h2>The service</h2>
      <p>
        NoWatermark provides free browser-based tools for inspecting and removing metadata from
        images and text. Processing happens on your device; we do not receive, store or process your
        files.
      </p>

      <h2>Your content and your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You must have the right to process any content you put into these tools. Removing
        provenance, attribution or copyright information from work you do not own may be unlawful in
        some jurisdictions, and may breach the terms of the platform you obtained it from.
        Responsibility for that rests with you.
      </p>

      <h2>No guarantee of undetectability</h2>
      <p>This is the most important thing on this page, so we will be direct about it.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          We do not guarantee that content processed with these tools is undetectable as
          AI-generated, by any detector, now or in future.
        </li>
        <li>
          The absence of a detected signal does not prove the absence of every watermark. Some
          watermarks — SynthID and statistical text watermarks among them — cannot be detected by
          any browser-based tool, so we can neither confirm nor deny their presence.
        </li>
        <li>
          Removing a C2PA manifest does not necessarily prevent provenance from being recovered.
          Durable Content Credentials can be re-associated with an image by a provider using an
          invisible watermark or content fingerprint held in their own systems.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Disclosure obligations remain yours</h2>
      <p>
        Platform rules, professional codes, and legal requirements around disclosing AI-generated
        content apply regardless of what metadata a file carries. Removing a metadata field does not
        remove an obligation to disclose.
      </p>

      <h2>Results are provided as-is</h2>
      <p>
        The tools are offered without warranty of any kind. Scan results are our best interpretation
        of the data present in a file and may be incomplete or, for malformed files, incorrect.
        Always keep your original file: our cleaners never modify it, and produce a separate copy.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Do not use these tools to facilitate fraud, impersonation, harassment, or the removal of
        ownership information from content belonging to other people.
      </p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any loss or damage arising
        from use of this site, including any consequence of relying on a scan result or of removing
        metadata from a file.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions can go to <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="h-16"></div>
</BaseLayout>
